# LF everywhere, in the repo and in the working copy.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) checks files out with
# CRLF. Biome formats to LF, so a fresh clone would fail `npm run verify` on
# line endings alone, having changed nothing. eol=lf takes that decision away
# from whatever git config the machine happens to have.
* text=auto eol=lf
